Bootstrap: docker
From: ubuntu:26.04

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROMACS 2022 fork (Vetrov-Anton/gromacs-dftbplus), branch `modernize`
#   base   : ubuntu 26.04 LTS / GCC 15.2 / cmake 4.2
#   + DFTB+  : QM/MM backend, linked via find_package(DftbPlus CONFIG)
#   + PLUMED : runtime-linked, so the PLUMED version is swappable after the
#              build just by pointing PLUMED_KERNEL somewhere else
#   + libtorch : so PLUMED can be built with --enable-libtorch
#
# This single file replaces vetrov_gmx_fixed.def.  What changed:
#
#   * DFTB+ IS NO LONGER PINNED TO 21.2.  The fork used to carry a copy of the
#     2020-era DFTB+ C API in qm_dftbplus.h, called the since-removed
#     dftbp_get_atom_list(), and imported libdftbplus.a/libdftd3.a/libmudpack.a
#     by explicit filename.  All three are gone (commit "DFTB+: use the
#     installed package..."), so this recipe no longer needs:
#         - DFTBPLUS_VERSION=21.2
#         - PATCH_PROCESS_INPUT and its two seds
#         - the three `sed 's/\.a/\.so/'` calls on src/programs/CMakeLists.txt
#         - CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS with -rpath-link
#     and GMX_QMMM_DFTBPLUS_LIB is now the install PREFIX, not <prefix>/lib.
#
#   * The sources come from the local working tree, not from GitHub, because
#     the DFTB+ modernisation lives in local commits.  See %files below.
#
# Kept from vetrov_gmx_fixed.def, each because it was verified to break
# otherwise:
#
#   1. `set -e -x` - without it the build "succeeds" and produces an image
#      with no /opt/gmx in it at all.
#   2. SRC=/opt/src, NOT /tmp - apptainer bind-mounts the HOST /tmp into the
#      build container, and leftovers from an earlier run make tar and
#      configure fail in ways that look like a broken compiler.
#   3. `file` is installed - FFTW's configure needs /usr/bin/file.
#   4. (no longer applies) Earlier recipes pinned ubuntu:20.04 (GCC 9) because
#      GCC 11 could not compile densityfitting.cpp: gmx::IndexGroupsAndNames is
#      only forward-declared in mdmodulenotification.h and GCC 11's
#      std::function constructor required a complete type.  libstdc++ dropped
#      that requirement after GCC 11.  Verified by compiling all of libgromacs
#      with ninja -k 0, so nothing stops at the first error:
#          ubuntu 24.04 / GCC 13.3 -> 869 targets, 0 compiler errors
#          ubuntu 26.04 / GCC 15.2 -> 872 targets, 0 compiler errors
#      densityfitting.cpp among them both times.  The base is now 26.04 LTS.
#
#      26.04 ships cmake 4.2.3, so this builds under CMake 4.  Nothing in the
#      tree blocks it: GROMACS declares cmake_minimum_required 3.13, and the
#      bundled subprojects that still declare < 3.5 are never processed -
#      tng_io comes in via include(BuildTNG.cmake) rather than
#      add_subdirectory(), and googletest/pybind need BUILD_TESTING/GMXAPI,
#      which are off here.  DFTB+ 24.1 and its submodules declare >= 3.9.
#   5. PLUMED is built ONCE, in runtime mode.  The old aozalevsky recipe built
#      2.7.4, linked GROMACS against it in `shared` mode, then deleted it and
#      dropped 2.9.0 at the same path - an unverifiable ABI gamble.  Runtime
#      linking removes the DT_NEEDED entry altogether.
#   6. -D__PLUMED_WRAPPER_CXX_BIND_C=0.  The fork does `plumedcmd = plumed_cmd;`
#      (a plain C function pointer).  From PLUMED 2.9 on, plumed_cmd is a macro
#      expanding to the overloaded C++ template PLMD::Plumed::plumed_cmd_cxx,
#      which has no address; the flag restores the plain C symbol.
#
# The QM/MM exclusion CODE is Vetrov's and is untouched: GMX_QMMM_NREXCL
# (0..3) and GMX_QMMM_FUDGEQQ are read at run time.  The fork's own default is
# 0 = no exclusions at all; this image overrides it to 3 in %environment, which
# is the setting that matches the Alexander-the-Evil fork.  See %help.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

%files
    # The DFTB+ modernisation is in local commits, so the tree is copied in
    # rather than cloned.  Change this path if the repository moves.
    /home/aav/Desktop/zlobin_gmx/vetrov_src /opt/src/gromacs-dftbplus

%post -c /bin/bash
    set -e -x
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # ------------------------- knobs (edit here) -----------------------
    NJOBS=6                        # 12 cores but only 7 GB RAM: g++ would OOM
    SRC=/opt/src                   # NOT /tmp: the host /tmp is bind-mounted in
    DFTBPLUS_VERSION=25.1          # any release with the modern C API (>=23.1)
    PLUMED_VERSION=2.10.1
    LIBTORCH_VERSION=2.12.1        # PLUMED 2.10 wants torch >= 2.7
    WITH_LIBTORCH=yes              # "no" skips libtorch and PLUMED's torch CVs
    PLUMED_MODE=runtime            # runtime | shared  (runtime recommended)
    # -------------------------------------------------------------------

    mkdir -p ${SRC}

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 1. Toolchain and libraries
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # a dropped connection mid-download must not kill an hour-long build
    apt-get update -y
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends -o Acquire::Retries=5 \
        ca-certificates wget git unzip xxd patch file \
        build-essential gfortran \
        cmake ninja-build \
        libopenblas-dev liblapack-dev \
        libgsl-dev zlib1g-dev libfftw3-dev \
        libopenmpi-dev openmpi-bin \
        python3 python3-dev \
        vim nano less htop
    # ubuntu 26.04 ships cmake 4.2.3.  The earlier pip install of a newer cmake
    # (needed on 20.04, which had only 3.16) is gone; pip on modern ubuntu is
    # PEP 668 "externally managed" and would refuse anyway.
    cmake --version
    gcc --version | head -1

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 2. DFTB+  ->  /opt/dftbplus
    #    Shared build with the C API on; GROMACS picks it up through
    #    /opt/dftbplus/lib/cmake/dftbplus/dftbplus-config.cmake
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    cd ${SRC}
    rm -rf dftbplus
    git clone --recursive --depth 1 -b ${DFTBPLUS_VERSION} \
        https://github.com/dftbplus/dftbplus.git
    cd dftbplus
    cmake -B _build -G Ninja \
        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/dftbplus \
        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
        -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON \
        -DWITH_API=ON \
        -DENABLE_DYNAMIC_LOADING=ON \
        -DWITH_TBLITE=ON \
        -DWITH_SDFTD3=ON \
        -DWITH_MPI=OFF \
        -DWITH_OMP=ON \
        -DWITH_PYTHON=OFF \
        -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF \
        -DHYBRID_CONFIG_METHODS="Submodule;Find;Fetch"
    cmake --build _build -- -j${NJOBS}
    cmake --install _build
    # find_package(DftbPlus CONFIG) needs exactly this file:
    test -f /opt/dftbplus/lib/cmake/dftbplus/dftbplus-config.cmake
    cd ${SRC} && rm -rf dftbplus

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 3. libtorch (optional, only for PLUMED's pytorch CVs)
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    if [ "${WITH_LIBTORCH}" = "yes" ]; then
        cd ${SRC}
        # The archive lost its "cxx11-abi-" infix around torch 2.8, when cxx11
        # became the only ABI: 2.2.0 exists only under the old name, 2.12.1 only
        # under the new one.  Try the modern name first and fall back, and check
        # the result - `wget -O` leaves a stub on a 404, which would otherwise
        # surface much later as a confusing unzip failure.
        LT_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/libtorch/cpu
        rm -f libtorch.zip
        for _n in "libtorch-shared-with-deps-${LIBTORCH_VERSION}%2Bcpu.zip" \
                  "libtorch-cxx11-abi-shared-with-deps-${LIBTORCH_VERSION}%2Bcpu.zip"; do
            if wget -q --no-check-certificate -O libtorch.zip "${LT_URL}/${_n}"; then
                echo "libtorch archive: ${_n}"
                break
            fi
            rm -f libtorch.zip
        done
        test -s libtorch.zip
        unzip -tq libtorch.zip
        cd /opt && unzip -q ${SRC}/libtorch.zip
        rm -f ${SRC}/libtorch.zip
    fi

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 4. PLUMED  ->  /opt/plumed   (built ONCE, in its final configuration)
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    cd ${SRC}
    wget -q --no-check-certificate \
        https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/releases/download/v${PLUMED_VERSION}/plumed-src-${PLUMED_VERSION}.tgz
    rm -rf plumed-${PLUMED_VERSION}
    tar xf plumed-src-${PLUMED_VERSION}.tgz
    cd plumed-${PLUMED_VERSION}

    PLUMED_CONF_EXTRA=""
    if [ "${WITH_LIBTORCH}" = "yes" ]; then
        # libtorch >= 1.13 needs C++17; this PLUMED's configure hardcodes C++14
        sed -i 's/c++14/c++17/' configure
        export CPATH=${CPATH:-}:/opt/libtorch/include/torch/csrc/api/include:/opt/libtorch/include
        export LIBRARY_PATH=${LIBRARY_PATH:-}:/opt/libtorch/lib
        export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}:/opt/libtorch/lib
        PLUMED_CONF_EXTRA="--enable-libtorch"
    fi
    export PYTHON_BIN=$(which python3)

    ./configure --prefix=/opt/plumed --enable-modules=all ${PLUMED_CONF_EXTRA}
    make -j${NJOBS}
    make install
    test -f /opt/plumed/lib/libplumedKernel.so
    cd ${SRC} && rm -rf plumed-${PLUMED_VERSION} plumed-src-${PLUMED_VERSION}.tgz

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 5. GROMACS fork (copied in by %files)
    #
    #    The sources are ALREADY plumed-patched (the #if (GMX_PLUMED) blocks
    #    are committed), so do NOT run `plumed patch`.  Only the three files
    #    that `plumed patch` would drop into the source root are needed:
    #      Plumed.h     - wrapper header, included as "../../../Plumed.h"
    #      Plumed.cmake - defines ${PLUMED_LOAD}, included by
    #                     src/gromacs/CMakeLists.txt when GMX_PLUMED=ON
    #      Plumed.inc   - only used by the (unused) GNU-make build
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    cd ${SRC}/gromacs-dftbplus
    git log -1 --format='building %H (%ad) %s' --date=short 2>/dev/null || \
        echo "building from a copied working tree (no .git)"
    rm -rf .git build

    PLUMED_PREFIX=/opt/plumed
    PLUMED_ROOT=${PLUMED_PREFIX}/lib/plumed
    ln -fs ${PLUMED_PREFIX}/include/plumed/wrapper/Plumed.h   Plumed.h
    ln -fs ${PLUMED_ROOT}/src/lib/Plumed.inc.${PLUMED_MODE}   Plumed.inc
    ln -fs ${PLUMED_ROOT}/src/lib/Plumed.cmake.${PLUMED_MODE} Plumed.cmake
    # the symlinks must RESOLVE - a dangling Plumed.h is what made the original
    # recipe die with "fatal error: ../../../Plumed.h: No such file or directory"
    test -e Plumed.h && test -e Plumed.inc && test -e Plumed.cmake

    mkdir -p build && cd build
    cmake .. \
        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/gmx \
        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
        -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-D__PLUMED_WRAPPER_CXX_BIND_C=0" \
        -DGMX_QMMM_PROGRAM=dftbplus \
        -DGMX_QMMM_DFTBPLUS_LIB=/opt/dftbplus \
        -DGMX_PLUMED=ON \
        -DGMX_DOUBLE=ON \
        -DGMX_MPI=ON \
        -DGMX_OPENMP=ON \
        -DGMX_GPU=OFF \
        -DGMX_DEFAULT_SUFFIX=OFF \
        -DGMXAPI=OFF \
        -DGMX_INSTALL_NBLIB_API=OFF \
        -DGMX_BUILD_OWN_FFTW=ON \
        -DGMX_BUILD_MANUAL=OFF \
        -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF \
        -DGMX_BUILD_UNITTESTS=OFF \
        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH_USE_LINK_PATH=ON \
        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH="/opt/dftbplus/lib;/opt/plumed/lib"
    make -j${NJOBS}
    make install
    cd ${SRC} && rm -rf gromacs-dftbplus

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 6. Cleanup
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    apt-get clean
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C
    export PATH=/opt/gmx/bin:/opt/plumed/bin:/opt/dftbplus/bin:${PATH}
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/gmx/lib:/opt/gmx/lib64:/opt/dftbplus/lib:/opt/plumed/lib:/opt/libtorch/lib:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}
    # PLUMED is runtime-linked: this is the only thing tying gmx to a PLUMED
    # build, so a different PLUMED needs no GROMACS rebuild.
    export PLUMED_KERNEL=/opt/plumed/lib/libplumedKernel.so
    export PLUMED_ROOT=/opt/plumed/lib/plumed
    # QM/MM electrostatics variant (0..4); 1 = full electrostatic QM/MM
    export GMX_QMMM_VARIANT=1
    export OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
    # Topological exclusions in the QM/MM electrostatics.  The fork defaults to
    # 0 (none); 3 excludes 1-2/1-3 neighbours and scales 1-4 pairs by fudgeQQ.
    # Override per run with --env GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=<0..3>.
    export GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=3

%runscript
    exec gmx "$@"

%test
    export PATH=/opt/gmx/bin:/opt/plumed/bin:${PATH}
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/gmx/lib:/opt/gmx/lib64:/opt/dftbplus/lib:/opt/plumed/lib:/opt/libtorch/lib:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}
    export PLUMED_KERNEL=/opt/plumed/lib/libplumedKernel.so
    gmx --version | head -20
    plumed info --version
    gmx mdrun -h 2>&1 | grep -q -- '-plumed' && echo "OK: gmx mdrun has -plumed"
    ldd /opt/gmx/lib/libgromacs.so | grep -qi dftb && echo "OK: libgromacs links DFTB+"
    ldd /opt/gmx/lib/libgromacs.so | grep -qi plumed && \
        echo "WARNING: libgromacs has a hard PLUMED dependency (expected: none)" || \
        echo "OK: no DT_NEEDED on PLUMED - kernel is dlopen'ed via PLUMED_KERNEL"

%labels
    Author      vvmas12@gmail.com
    BasedOn     Arthur Zalevsky <aozalevsky@gmail.com>
    GROMACS     2022 fork, Vetrov-Anton/gromacs-dftbplus, branch modernize
    QMMM        DFTB+ (any version with the modern C API)
    PLUMED      runtime-linked

%help
    GROMACS 2022 (double precision, OpenMPI) with DFTB+ QM/MM and PLUMED,
    built from the Vetrov fork with the DFTB+ interface modernised.

    Build
    -----
        apptainer build --fakeroot gmx-vetrov.sif vetrov_gmx_dftb_plumed.def

    The GROMACS sources are copied from the host path in %files, not cloned,
    because the DFTB+ modernisation lives in local commits on branch
    `modernize`.  To roll back to the untouched fork:  git checkout
    vetrov-original.

    Run
    ---
        apptainer exec gmx-vetrov.sif gmx grompp -f md.mdp -c c.gro -p t.top -o md.tpr
        apptainer exec gmx-vetrov.sif mpirun -np 1 gmx mdrun -deffnm md -plumed plumed.dat

    QM/MM exclusions - READ THIS
    ----------------------------
    THIS IMAGE SETS GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=3 IN %environment.  That is NOT the fork's
    own default - built from bare sources this code applies no topological
    exclusions at all, and every MM atom within the cut-off polarizes the QM
    density, bonded neighbours included.  The override is deliberate: 3 is the
    setting that reproduces the Alexander-the-Evil fork, which applies
    exclusions unconditionally.

        GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=0              no exclusions (the fork's own default,
                                       NOT this image's)
        GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=1|2|3          exclude up to 1-2 / 1-3 / 1-4 neighbours;
                                       1-4 pairs are scaled by fudgeQQ
        GMX_QMMM_FUDGEQQ=<x>           override the force field's fudgeQQ

    mdrun prints which one is in effect; check that line before trusting a run:

        Topological exclusions applied to the QM/MM electrostatics
        (GMX_QMMM_NREXCL = 3).

    To get the fork's bare behaviour back:  --env GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=0

    Other notes
    -----------
      * DFTB+ needs a dftb_in.hsd in the working directory, and since
        dftbp_get_atom_list() is gone from the C API, the QM atom ORDER there
        must match the QM group of the .mdp.  Slater-Koster parameter sets
        (e.g. 3ob-3-1) are NOT bundled - fetch them from dftb.org.

      * MIGRATING A dftb_in.hsd FROM DFTB+ 21.2.  An input written for 21.2
        fails twice against 24.1, both times inside DFTB+, not GROMACS:

            Analysis { CalculateForces = Yes }

        is no longer a known key - the parser reports "1 node(s) have been
        ignored" and then halts.  Deleting the line gets past the parser but
        the run then dies after the SCC with

            Forces not available, you must initialise your calculator with
            forces enabled.

        In 24.1 the key is PrintForces, and it is what switches force
        evaluation on for the API.  So replace the line with:

            Analysis { PrintForces = Yes }

        With that one change the QM/MM energies are unchanged: on the
        ~/diala_QMMM inputs with GMX_QMMM_NREXCL=3 this image reproduces the
        DFTB+ 21.2 build exactly - Quantum En. -3.90686e+05, Potential
        -1.00558e+06.
      * GMX_QMMM_VARIANT selects the QM/MM electrostatics scheme (0..4);
        preset to 1 here.
      * Legacy GROMACS QM/MM has no domain decomposition - use a single rank.
      * Swapping PLUMED without rebuilding GROMACS:
            apptainer exec -B /my/plumed:/my/plumed \
                --env PLUMED_KERNEL=/my/plumed/lib/libplumedKernel.so \
                gmx-vetrov.sif gmx mdrun ...
      * PLUMED here is the fork's own integration, unchanged, frozen at the
        PLUMED 2.5.1 feature level: no HREX, no -rerun under PLUMED, no
        expanded-ensemble or FEP-lambda CV. Ordinary biasing - metadynamics,
        walls, restraints, plain replica exchange - is unaffected.
